-- title:
--   Executable local-parameter selection fits a single exponential time envelope
-- statement:
--   For any natural number $h$, let $T_{\mathrm{par}}(h)$ be the time budget of the local-parameter procedure, including computation of the local counts, selection of the local prime, calculation of the bucket cap by division, and fixed overhead. Then
--   $$T_{\mathrm{par}}(h)\le2^{2048(h+1)+2}.$$
--
--   This finite estimate accounts for the executable parameter-selection phase in the overall local-cover resource analysis, including the case $h=0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LocalParameterBounds.lean#L89-L101

